;; NOTE (reclassification, see rec-forward-reference-taxonomy.md):
;; `rec { x = y; y = 1; }.x` used to live here as an "error" case, but it is a
;; VALID forward reference (Nix = 1). It only appeared to be an accepted error
;; because every lane held: the evaluator held on a rec forward-reference BUG
;; (:unbound-var), while the clj-meta/px-runtime lanes held at their forward-ref
;; frontier (they also hold on the valid `let a = b + 1; b = 10; in a`). Once the
;; evaluator resolves rec forward references correctly, the lanes no longer agree
;; on an error, so this case no longer belongs in the error-agreement corpus. It
;; is now covered by the forward-reference frontier corpus.
